/// GroceryOCR Project Documentation
///
/// Overview:
/// GroceryOCR is an iOS app that allows users to scan grocery ingredient lists using the camera, extract text via OCR, and export the processed data as a CSV file. The app also enables users to manage and organize scanned data within the app.
///
/// This document provides an overview of the core Swift files, their functionality, and how they interact.
import Foundation
/// ImagePicker.swift
///
/// Purpose:
/// Provides a SwiftUI wrapper around UIImagePickerController to allow users to capture images using the camera.
///
/// Key Components:
/// - UIViewControllerRepresentable: Enables SwiftUI to use UIKit's UIImagePickerController.
/// - makeUIViewController: Initializes and configures UIImagePickerController.
/// - updateUIViewController: Required for UIViewControllerRepresentable but not used.
/// - makeCoordinator: Creates a delegate to handle image selection.
/// - Coordinator: A helper class to manage the selection and dismissal of the picker.
/// OCRHelper.swift
///
/// Purpose:
/// Uses Apple’s Vision framework to recognize text from images and extract ingredient lists.
///
/// Key Components:
/// - recognizeText(from:completion:):
///   - Uses VNRecognizeTextRequest to process the image.
///   - Extracts text from recognized observations.
///   - Calls the completion handler with the extracted text.
/// How It Works:
/// 1. Converts the UIImage to CGImage.
/// 2. Performs text recognition with VNImageRequestHandler.
/// 3. Extracts text and returns it via a closure.
/// CSVHelper.swift
///
/// Purpose:
/// Handles storing and exporting scanned ingredients.
///
/// Key Components:
/// - saveScannedText(_:): Appends a new scan to storage.
/// - loadScannedText() -> [String]: Loads stored scans from UserDefaults.
/// - saveToUserDefaults(data:): Saves ingredient lists persistently.
/// - saveToCSV(data:): Writes scanned data to a CSV file.
/// - exportCSV(): Allows users to share the CSV file via UIActivityViewController.
/// - getDocumentsDirectory(): Returns the app's document directory.
/// How It Works:
/// 1. Scanned ingredients are stored in UserDefaults.
/// 2. On export, stored ingredients are written to a CSV file.
/// 3. The file is shared via the standard iOS share sheet.
/// ContentView.swift
///
/// Purpose:
/// The main UI for the app, allowing users to:
/// - Capture an image.
/// - Extract text from the image.
/// - View and manage extracted ingredients.
/// - Export the final list as a CSV file.
/// Key Components:
/// - @State properties:
///   - image: Stores the captured image.
///   - extractedText: Holds the OCR-extracted text.
///   - storedScans: Stores previously scanned ingredients.
/// - deleteScan(_:): Removes an ingredient from the list and updates storage.
/// - Floating buttons for key actions:
///   - Camera: Opens the image picker.
///   - OCR: Extracts text from the image.
///   - Export: Saves and shares the CSV.
/// How It Works:
/// 1. Users capture an image using ImagePicker.
/// 2. The OCR process extracts text from the image.
/// 3. The text is added to a persistent ingredient list.
/// 4. Users can delete, edit, or export the list as a CSV.
